    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "GPT-5.6 Sol on levin-2015-girardia-10: partially-resolvable, resolvability 0.57";
    dc:description "Existing measurements can distinguish gross toxicity from organized regeneration. They cannot fully discriminate an instructive gap-junction mechanism from selective toxicity or other off-target perturbations.";
    dc:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/dataset-resolvability-0.2.0>;
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Proposed test with existing data: Quantify survival, regeneration completion, disorder metrics, and clustering of blinded head shapes after octanol versus toxicity controls. Discrete coherent outcomes with normal viability would weigh against generalized toxicity but would not exclude selective off-target effects.";
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-resolvability-assessor-gpt-5.6-sol-medium>;
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/assessmentType> "dataset-resolvability/0.2.0";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/evidenceAgainst> "Coherence does not uniquely imply instructive signaling.", "No intermediate morphologies is sensitive to sample size and classification.", "Octanol has possible targets beyond gap junctions.";
